---
import Base from "~/layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "~/data/site";
const updated = "5 September 2026";
---
<Base
  title="Terms of service | MyWebMaster"
  description="The terms on which MyWebMaster provides Autopilot: what we do, what we do not change, ownership of work, the guarantee, cancellation and limits of liability."
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: "Terms", href: "/legal/terms/" }]}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow prose">
      <p class="label">Legal</p>
      <h1>Terms of service</h1>
      <p class="mono muted">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <h2>1. What we provide</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name} provides {site.product}, a monthly service that watches a website, makes
        certain agreed kinds of change to it, and reports on the results. Exactly which changes
        are allowed on each plan is published at
        <a href="/what-it-changes/">what it changes</a>, and that page forms part of these terms.
      </p>

      <h2>2. What we will never change</h2>
      <p>
        We will never automatically change your prices, your guarantees, your legal wording,
        factual claims about your business, or the settings that control whether search engines
        are allowed to show your site. This applies on every plan and cannot be waived even by
        agreement, because it protects both of us.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Access and control</h2>
      <p>
        You give us the access we need to make changes to your website, and permission to view
        your Google search figures and visitor statistics. Wherever possible that view-only
        access is exactly that. You can withdraw any of it at any time, and you can stop all
        automatic activity immediately with a single instruction.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Ownership</h2>
      <p>
        Everything we produce — the changes, the wording, the settings and the full record of
        what was done — belongs to you from the moment it is made. We do not license anything
        back to you, and nothing is kept in a system you lose access to when you leave. Before we
        make any change we take a complete copy of your website as it stands, and we keep it for
        as long as you are a client. On leaving you may keep the improved site, or ask us to
        restore that original copy.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Measurement and the guarantee</h2>
      <p>
        On the Compound plan we improve one group of pages and deliberately leave a similar
        group untouched, then compare the two over a fixed 28-day period. If the untouched pages
        perform better than the improved ones across two of those periods in a row, we refund
        the fee for the second month. The guarantee covers that comparison only; it is not a
        promise about your total visitor numbers or revenue.
      </p>

      <h2>6. What we cannot promise</h2>
      <p>
        Where you appear in search results is decided by companies whose systems we do not
        control. We do not promise particular positions, visitor numbers or revenue, and anyone
        who does is promising something they cannot deliver. What we promise is the method, full
        visibility of what we did, and honest measurement of whether it worked.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Cancellation</h2>
      <p>
        Watch and Apply can be cancelled at any time, ending at the close of the month you have
        paid for. Compound runs for a minimum of three months, because comparing improved pages
        against untouched ones needs a full month to run and a little longer to report on.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Liability</h2>
      <p>
        Our total liability in connection with this service is limited to the fees you paid in
        the three months before whatever went wrong. Nothing here limits liability for death,
        personal injury or fraud. Because every change is recorded separately and can be undone,
        our first response to any mistake is simply to put it back.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Governing law</h2>
      <p>These terms are governed by the law of England and Wales.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  h1 { margin-block: 1rem 0.5rem; }
  .prose h2 { margin-top: 2.2em; font-size: var(--step-1); }
  .prose a { color: var(--accent); }
  code { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.88em; background: var(--bg-soft); padding: 0.1em 0.35em; border-radius: 3px; }
</style>
